d Farmers Market at 150 West 8th Street and documents its permanent canopy and vendor-stall market space.","source_url":"https://www.hollandfarmersmarket.com/market-history/","source_title":"Market History","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Market operation is schedule-dependent; consult the official calendar before visiting. Dogs are not permitted except service animals.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hope-holland-lemonjellos-coffee","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Lemonjello's Coffee","title":"Pair Coffee with Local Music","subtitle":"East 9th Street corridor — near College Avenue","notes":"Walk one block north from campus, then check the posted music calendar before choosing a drink or snack at the counter.","short_summary":"An independent coffeehouse combining a café counter with music programming.","evidence_claim":"Lemonjello’s official site describes the business as a coffee and music venue, while Downtown Holland’s dining guide lists it at 61 East 9th Street.","source_url":"https://lemonjellos.com/","source_title":"Lemonjello's | Coffee. Music. Life.","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Public café access; verify current operating hours and event details on the business site before going.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hope-holland-cappon-house","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Cappon House","title":"Tour a Mayor’s 1874 Home","subtitle":"West 9th Street corridor — west of Pine Avenue","notes":"Start at the visitor center and join a scheduled tour to see rooms interpreted around Isaac Cappon and his family.","short_summary":"A preserved mayoral residence interpreted to approximately 1900.","evidence_claim":"Holland Museum lists Cappon House at 228 W. 9th Street and identifies it as the 1874 home of Holland’s first mayor, restored in part to its circa-1900 appearance.","source_url":"https://hollandmuseum.org/venue/cappon-house/","source_title":"Cappon House","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Seasonal guided tours begin at the Cappon House Visitor Center; off-season visits require advance arrangements.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hope-holland-settlers-house","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Settlers House","title":"Compare a Working-Family Home","subtitle":"West 9th Street corridor — near Washington Avenue","notes":"Visit on the paired historic-house tour and compare this compact 1871 interpretation with the nearby Cappon House.","short_summary":"A small surviving home interpreted through Holland’s working-class history.","evidence_claim":"Holland Museum lists Settlers House at 190 W. 9th Street and says the circa-1867 building survived the 1871 fire and is restored to an 1871 appearance.","source_url":"https://hollandmuseum.org/venue/settlers-house/","source_title":"Settlers House","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Seasonal tours start at the nearby Cappon House Visitor Center; appointments are required outside the stated season.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hope-holland-holland-armory","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"The Holland Armory","title":"See the National Guard Exhibit","subtitle":"West 9th Street corridor — just west of River Avenue","notes":"Call the Holland Museum before going; the Armory’s National Guard exhibition is free but available by appointment.","short_summary":"A former civic and military building with a focused local National Guard display.","evidence_claim":"Holland Museum places The Holland Armory at 16 W. 9th Street and states that its 1921–1998 National Guard exhibition is free to visit by appointment.","source_url":"https://hollandmuseum.org/venue/the-armory/","source_title":"The Holland Armory","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The exhibition is free but appointment-only; call the Holland Museum at the number on the official page to arrange access.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hope-holland-city-hall","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Holland City Hall","title":"Locate the Civic Centerpiece","subtitle":"South River Avenue corridor — opposite Centennial Park","notes":"Use the River Avenue façade as a visual anchor, then cross toward Centennial Park for a closer look at the civic core.","short_summary":"A named municipal landmark anchoring the River Avenue civic block.","evidence_claim":"The City of Holland’s official facilities directory lists City Hall at 270 S River Avenue.","source_url":"https://www.cityofholland.com/Facilities?clear=False","source_title":"Facilities","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Exterior viewing is public; interior access is limited to municipal business hours and public meetings or services.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hope-holland-caboose-a967","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Pere Marquette Caboose No. A967","title":"Find the 1941 Caboose","subtitle":"Lincoln Avenue corridor — at the Padnos Transportation Center","notes":"Continue north on Lincoln Avenue to photograph the restored rail car beside the active transportation center.","short_summary":"A museum-operated railroad artifact displayed beside Holland’s passenger station.","evidence_claim":"Holland Museum identifies Pere Marquette Caboose No. A967 as a 1941 rail car located at the Padnos Transportation Center, 171 Lincoln Avenue.","source_url":"https://hollandmuseum.org/","source_title":"Holland Museum","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The exterior display is at an active transportation center; remain in public pedestrian areas and do not enter rail operating space.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
